#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md:18
msgid ""
"C++ includes a number of features that don't exist in C with an FFI impact:"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md:20
msgid ""
"Overloading: Overloads become impossible to express because of name mangling"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md:22
msgid ""
"Exceptions: Must catch exceptions at the FFI boundary and convert them to "
"error codes, as escaping exceptions in `extern \"C\"` functions constitute "
"undefined behavior"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md:26
msgid ""
"Destructors: C callers won't run destructors; must expose explicit "
"`*_destroy()` functions"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md:29
msgid ""
"Non-POD types: Must use opaque pointers across the FFI boundary as pass by "
"value does not make sense"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/ffi/language-differences/cpp-and-c.md:32
msgid ""
"Templates: Cannot expose directly; must instantiate explicitly and wrap each "
"specialization"
msgstr ""
